@namespace IzzyBlazor
@typeparam TItem
@attribute [CascadingTypeParameter(nameof(TItem))]
@inherits TableViewBase<TItem>
@attribute [ModeSupport(NoScript = ModeLevel.Partial, NoScriptNotes = "With JavaScript off, there's no select-all checkbox, and filters apply when you press Apply, not as you type; empty filters stay in the address (?f-customer=), as with any GET form.")]

@*
    A data table that sorts and pages through the URL: column headers and page numbers are
    links that set ?sort= and ?page=, so it works on static pages with no script, survives
    reloads, and can be shared. On interactive pages the links are ordinary navigations (with
    enhanced navigation the server renders the page again) and the table follows the URL.

    Filterable columns add a filter button to their header, opening the filter in a popover; the
    active filters show as removable tags above the table. Text matches anywhere, enums and
    booleans offer a menu, dates match a day, and numbers take a range (at least, at most).
    Filters go in the URL too (?f-customer=ada, ?f-total-min=100): with no script the fields
    submit a GET form when you press Enter or Apply; with script they apply as you type. The
    table filters by column values; operators, several conditions and a filter row belong to a
    data grid.

    Bind Sort, Page or Filter (@bind-Sort, @bind-Page, @bind-Filter) on an interactive page to
    keep them in the component instead: headers and page numbers become buttons, the URL doesn't change, and the
    table sorts and pages in place, like a client-side grid. It starts from the URL's values. The
    bound Filter is the filter tree (Filter.All of a FieldFilter per filtered column); conditions
    set in C# that a column's panel can't show still apply, as tags of their own.

    Give it Items (a list, or an IQueryable that EF Core translates) and it sorts and pages them,
    or an ItemsProvider to load each page yourself: it gets a DataRequest (the range, the sort, the
    filter tree, the columns as fields) and returns a DataResult. If loading fails, the table logs
    the exception and shows "Couldn't load the rows." with Retry in place of the rows (a link to
    the same address on static pages); with Load more, the rows shown stay and the message goes
    under them.

    Paging pages by cursor, for data with no total or that pages by a token: the provider returns
    the items and a Next cursor (DataResult.Next), and the table shows First, Previous and Next
    (NextPrevious), or loads as the last row comes into view (LoadOnScroll, best with a
    MaxHeight). The cursor goes in the URL (?cursor=) beside ?page=, the page's position.
    Loading on scroll adds a page as the last row comes into view: in place on interactive pages,
    and on static pages through a "Load more" link under the rows (?page=3 shows the first three),
    which the script follows and enhanced navigation swaps in. With script off the link shows.

    SelectionMode adds a checkbox (Multiple) or radio button (Single) per row: it posts the row's
    ItemKey with the surrounding form, and @bind-Selection follows it. RowHref makes each row a link. Columns
    take FooterText or Footer for a footer row.

    <Table Items="orders" PageSize="10" Caption="Orders">
        <PropertyColumn Property="o => o.Customer" Sortable />
        <PropertyColumn Property="o => o.Total" Format="C" Sortable />
        <TemplateColumn Title="Status"><Badge>@context.Status</Badge></TemplateColumn>
    </Table>

    Accessibility:
    - `Caption` names the table for screen readers; it isn't shown. It also names the scrolling
      area, which can be scrolled from the keyboard; with script it's a Tab stop only while it
      has something to scroll.
    - Sortable headers are links, and the sorted column has `aria-sort`.
    - Each filter button is named for its column ("Filter Customer"), and so is the field in its
      panel, by a visible label. The active filters are a group named "Filters".
    - Row checkboxes are named "Select" and the row's `RowLabel` ("Select order 1001"); without
      one, the `ItemKey`.
    - The range under the table ("1–5 of 23") is read when it changes.
    - A failed load is announced from a status region that's always in the table ("Couldn't
      load the rows."); the message shows with Retry after it. Focus stays where it was, and
      goes to the table's scroll box once Retry brings the rows.
*@

<ib-table @attributes="AdditionalAttributes" class="@_class" style="@_style" data-ib-page-key="@(HasFilters && !UseState ? PageKey : null)" data-ib-cursor-key="@(HasFilters && !UseState && CursorPaging ? CursorKey : null)" data-ib-load-on-scroll="@(Paging == DataPaging.LoadOnScroll ? "" : null)" data-ib-interactive="@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "" : null)">
    @Body
</ib-table>

@code {
    /// <inheritdoc />
    internal override string ViewName => "Table";
}
